KT412 (Dongwon DW02-412H) — ath9k 2.4G driver ceiling = 30.0 dBm.

Persistent OpenWrt kernel patch (applied by quilt on every target/linux
prepare, so it survives the full `make` — unlike a post-prepare sed).

Two changes, both driver-source only (ART/EEPROM/caldata are NEVER touched):
  1) ath9k_hw_set_power_per_rate_table(): drop the CTL regulatory edge clamp
     on the 2.4G target power so the per-rate target is not pulled below the
     forced ceiling.
  2) ath9k_hw_ar9300_set_txpower(): force every per-rate target power
     (targetPowerValT2[]) up to at least 60 half-dB = 30.0 dBm, band-wide,
     so iw phy / iwinfo / debugfs advertise 30.0 dBm on every 2.4G channel
     (1..11). This is a TEST/extreme build: conducted RF above the PA's
     ~25-26 dBm saturation is clipped/non-clean — see /root/POWER-REPORT.txt
     and /root/RF-SOLUTION.txt for the honest RF/EIRP picture.

Marker: KT412-30dbm (build gate requires exactly 2 occurrences post-compile).

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/ar9003_eeprom.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath9k/ar9003_eeprom.c
@@ -5347,7 +5347,7 @@
 			}
 		}
 
-		minCtlPower = (u8)min(twiceMaxEdgePower, scaledPower);
+		minCtlPower = scaledPower; /* KT412-30dbm */
 
 		ath_dbg(common, REGULATORY,
 			"SEL-Min ctlMode %d pCtlMode %d 2xMaxEdge %d sP %d minCtlPwr %d\n",
@@ -5510,7 +5510,7 @@
 		}
 	}
 
-	regulatory->max_power_level = 0;
+	{ int _k; printk_once(KERN_INFO "KT412-30DBM-PATCH-ACTIVE: forcing 2.4G targetPowerValT2 to 60 (30.0 dBm)\n"); for (_k = 0; _k < ar9300RateSize; _k++) if (targetPowerValT2[_k] < 60) targetPowerValT2[_k] = 60; } /* KT412-30dbm */ regulatory->max_power_level = 0;
 	for (i = 0; i < ar9300RateSize; i++) {
 		if (targetPowerValT2[i] > regulatory->max_power_level)
 			regulatory->max_power_level = targetPowerValT2[i];
